  "pp_id": "13776339",
  "development_type": "Minor dwellings",
  "description": "Erection of a detached bungalow in the rear garden with associated car parking and refuse bins.",
  "site_name": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposal would provide self-contained residential units within the curtilage of existing houses, that would not have regard to the internal space standards and would be in conflict with other Local Plan policies. The proposal would be unacceptable in principle and would fail to comply with Local Plan policy SC1 (Housing Growth).",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposal, by reason of its cramped and inadequate internal space, and poor outlook from the proposed habitable windows, would fail to provide an acceptable standard of accommodation for future occupiers, contrary to Local Plan policies SC5 and London Plan policy D6.  ",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposal, by reason of its inappropriate layout and design, would result in bulky, incongruous and unbalanced development that would fail to reflect character and appearance of the surrounding area and provide an acceptable street frontage. It is contrary to Local Plan policies CC1 (Context and character), CC2 (Urban design and architecture) SC1 (Housing Growth) and SC4 (Scale and intensity of new housing development) and London Plan Policies D4 (Delivering good design) and D6 (Housing quality and standards).",
    "Reason : 4 - The applicant has failed to demonstrate that the proposal would not result in harm to highway and pedestrian safety, contrary to Local Plan policy EC2 (Developing a Sustainable Local Transport Network) and the Residential Crossovers and Off-Street Parking Policy."
  ],
